# 07-memory-model.md §11.5 at INSTANTIATION. `inout $T` is legal to write -- the
# rule is about what T becomes -- so this one cannot be decided at the template
# and is checked where the binding is chosen: tychoc's instantiate_generic and
# tychoc0's mono_instantiate, both reporting the CALL line. Phase 39: before the
# fix both compilers accepted, compiled and ran this. Both reject (differential).
fn f(c: inout $T) -> int:
    return 1

fn main():
    ch := channel(int, 2)
    println(str(f(&ch)))
